CORE dfcc-only
main.c
--dfcc main --enforce-contract release --enforce-contract acquire
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^\[.*\] .*: FAILURE$
--
The calls pass more arguments than the library's malloc and free take. The
write set has to bind to the write set parameter, which follows the
parameters of the definition, rather than be appended after the surplus
arguments, where it bound to M_DEVBUF and made allocation and deallocation
fail the write set checks.
